-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9","T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'Writing an fstab entry for a mount point REMOVES any pre-existing entry ... exactly one entry afterwards'","AC2: 'The prior fstab is backed up before modification, so a bad edit is recoverable from the host itself'","Absence: neither AC states the rewrite is performed atomically (temp-file + rename) so a partial write cannot leave the live /etc/fstab in a corrupt intermediate state"],"finding":"AC1/AC2 specify removing the stale entry and backing up the prior fstab, but the plan does not state that the fstab rewrite itself is atomic (e.g. write-to-temp-then-rename). An in-place edit interrupted mid-write (crash/power loss during the remove-then-append) could leave a truncated or malformed fstab; the backup enables manual recovery but recovery is not automatic and boot could be affected.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f95bb14af5f2712e3","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC1/AC2 (F3)","norm_id":"n25e8a726b8ad876e","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A crash or interruption during the remove-then-write mutation of /etc/fstab leaves a truncated file; next boot mounts (or fails to mount) unexpectedly and recovery requires an operator to restore the backup by hand"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC (or extend AC1) requiring the fstab mutation to build the new content in a temp file and atomically `mv` it into place, and assert in the test that the operation is atomic.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State a one-line positive rationale for the F3 approach (in-place remove-by-mount-point + pre-edit backup) — e.g. why it is preferred over a delimited managed-block rewrite or systemd .mount units.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'Writing an fstab entry for a mount point REMOVES any pre-existing entry for that same mount point that is not the current UUID'","AC2: 'The prior fstab is backed up before modification, so a bad edit is recoverable from the host itself with no network' — states WHAT but not WHY this approach was chosen over alternatives","The chosen approach IS defensible (minimal, codebase-aligned, backed by AC2's recovery guarantee); the gap is only the missing positive rationale, so this is minor."],"finding":"The F3 fix (AC1/AC2) is the only defect with a real design choice — in-place fstab surgery that removes prior entries for a mount point and appends the current one — yet the plan states no POSITIVE rationale for choosing this over structural alternatives (e.g. a delimited managed-block rewrite or systemd .mount units).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1b28707dae705415","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC1/AC2 (F3), plan section 'Acceptance criteria'","norm_id":"ne9e60cd1c79cd961","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future maintainer weighing whether to migrate gate-scratch/gerrit mounts to systemd .mount units cannot tell from the plan why in-place fstab editing was preferred and whether the backup is the load-bearing safety net"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"2084c607242b7c83","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["ed5fdea60d9d7144",5320],"description_boxes":["7879981d4f226a8f",0],"file_impact":["1764a9aefbfe8abc",2],"ticket_id":["2d54762b8a2a57fd",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":250934,"cache_write_tokens":171261,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":11217.5,"input_tokens":443526,"llm_calls":30,"llm_ms":163767.7,"output_tokens":18555,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":197502.2,"verify_requests":5},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","priority_floor":0.8,"provider_provenance":{"candidates":["bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6"],"capabiliti